  Disorders with the same sign in both cohorts: 5 / 5
  Note 1: absolute scores are not comparable across cohorts (different numbers of usable sites shift them as a whole); 
        only the standardised difference within each cohort is used here.
  Note 2: the model of this section is not adjusted for cell fractions - smoking itself affects cell composition, and removing composition
        as a covariate would remove part of the smoking effect.
  Note 3: the smoking score of the paediatric cohort should not be read as true smoking exposure; the sites of the score also
        respond to inflammation and other factors, and large differences must be understood accordingly.

